## 4. PANEL TAB ONE: PUBLISH GAME

The administrator must be able to publish their own games directly, without waiting for user approval.

Create a complete publishing form.

Required fields:

- Game title.
- Game description.
- APK file.

Optional field:

- Version number.

The only permitted game package upload must be an APK file.

Do not accept ZIP, HTML, EXE, MSI, AAB, IPA, or other file types as game packages.

Do not add a second package-upload option.

Use a generated application icon based on the game title rather than requiring an additional cover-image upload.

### Publishing form functionality

The administrator must be able to:

1. Enter a game title.
2. Write a description.
3. Enter an optional version number.
4. Select an APK file from their device.
5. See the selected filename and file size.
6. Cancel or replace the selected file before publishing.
7. Submit the publishing form.
8. See real upload progress.
9. Cancel an upload when safe and supported.
10. Receive a clear success or error message.

Validate required fields both in the frontend and backend.

Trim unnecessary whitespace.

Reject empty titles and descriptions.

Apply configurable limits to title length and description length.

Validate the APK extension, actual uploaded content, file size, and supported upload format on the server.

Do not trust the filename or MIME type alone.

Where supported, verify APK archive structure and the presence of expected Android package contents. Never execute uploaded APK files on the server.

Set a configurable maximum APK size that respects the actual hosting provider's limits. Show an understandable error when a file exceeds that limit.

Prevent accidental duplicate submissions caused by repeated clicks.

Disable the submit button while the operation is in progress.

Only mark a game as published after its file has been uploaded successfully and its database record has been created successfully.

If part of the operation fails, clean up incomplete uploads when possible and explain how the administrator can retry.

### After publishing

When the administrator successfully publishes a game:

- Save the APK in permanent object storage.
- Save the game's metadata in the database.
- Mark the game as published.
- Make it appear in Apps automatically.
- Generate a unique game ID.
- Record its publication date.
- Record its file size.
- Record the administrator who published it.
- Make it available through the authenticated download flow.
- Show a confirmation message.
- Reset the form after confirmed success.

The game must remain available after page refreshes, browser restarts, and future visits.

Never publish a game record pointing to a missing or inaccessible file.

## 5. PANEL TAB TWO: GAME APPROVALS

This section manages games submitted by ordinary registered users.

Display actual pending submissions from the database.

For each submission, show:

- Game title.
- Game description.
- Submitter's registered email address, visible only to authorized administrators.
- Submission date.
- APK file size.
- Version number when provided.
- Current review status.
- Available review actions.

